    OPT_keepMenu = "Right click stays “Menu”",
    OPT_keepMenu_TIP = "What you get: a plain right click on Blizzard's player, party and raid frames always opens the menu. If something else is there – for example after right-clicking a line in Blizzard's “Click Casting” window –, ezHeal puts “Menu” back, removes what was there and names it in chat. Checked at login, after closing Blizzard's window, after “Undo”, after loading a profile and after switching your talent group, out of combat only. Spells and macros on right click with Shift, Ctrl or Alt and on all other keys stay; a moved “Menu” comes back from its key. If “Target” is on right click and left click is taken, ezHeal only says so. If another addon handles click casting, ezHeal stays out of it. Off: right click can be bound freely; if “Menu” is missing, ezHeal says so once in chat.",
    OPT_noAutoSelfCast = "Self Cast off by default",
    OPT_noAutoSelfCast_TIP = "Switches Blizzard's “Self Cast” from “Auto” to “Key Press”: if a group member is out of range, you no longer heal yourself – you get Blizzard's message or the targeting cursor (with a group member as your target the spell goes to your target). This applies to the whole game, your action bars too; with the self cast key (Alt by default) you still cast on yourself. If you change “Self Cast” yourself in Blizzard's settings afterwards, your choice stays; if it is back on “Auto” by itself at login, ezHeal switches it again and says so. Turning this off brings back your old setting. Out of combat only, otherwise right after.",
    OPT_SELFCAST = "Blizzard's self cast",
    OPT_SELFCAST_BUTTON = "Open option",
